{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SignSequence"],"declarations":37,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.nineTenths_exponent_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.nineTenths_exponent_one","kind":"theorem","line":595,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L595-L606","doc":"…and the **exponent** form on the same real, discharging its extra `gapₙ ≤ 1`\nhypothesis too. `n = 2`, `k = 2`, `t = 1`: the run is exactly long enough for exponent `1`.\n\nOnly `t = 1` here, which is the exponent every real has for free — `9/10` is rational and\nhas no long runs to give more. That is the honest witness: it shows the theorem *applies*,\nnot that this `α` is interesting. A witness with `t ≥ 2` would need a real chosen for its\nrun structure, which is the number theory this lane deliberately does not attempt. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.nineTenths_run_approximates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.nineTenths_run_approximates","kind":"theorem","line":586,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L586-L592","doc":"The headline instantiated on that real: a dyadic of denominator `4` approximating\n`9/10` to within `gap₂ / 4`. Discharges every hypothesis of\n`expansion_run_approximates`, which is what makes it applicable rather than merely true. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_nineTenths_runs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_nineTenths_runs","kind":"theorem","line":572,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L572-L583","doc":"A real whose expansion genuinely plus-runs, so the run hypothesis is satisfiable at\n`k = 2` and not only at `k = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_half_flags","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_half_flags","kind":"theorem","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L555-L559","doc":"…and both bound flags are genuinely set there, so `Brackets` is a real constraint at\nthat state rather than two vacuous implications. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_half_bracketed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_half_bracketed","kind":"theorem","line":548,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L548-L552","doc":"The expansion of a concrete real reaches the bisection regime — so `Bracketed` is a\ncondition the expansion actually meets, not a hypothesis that is never discharged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.approx_exponent_of_run","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.approx_exponent_of_run","kind":"theorem","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L508-L535","doc":"**A run of `k ≥ n·t` signs gives approximation exponent `t`.**\n\nThe conclusion is the Diophantine form: an explicit rational of denominator `q = 2ⁿ` with\nerror at most `1 / qᵗ`. The run length is what supplies `t`; the bisection rate alone\nsupplies only `t = 1`, which every real has for free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expansion_run_approximates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expansion_run_approximates","kind":"theorem","line":472,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L472-L492","doc":"**A run of `k` in `α`'s expansion gives a dyadic of denominator `2ⁿ` accurate to\n`gapₙ / 2ᵏ`.**\n\nDenominator fixed by `n`; accuracy improving with `k`. That is the decoupling an\napproximation exponent above `1` consists of, now stated for a *given* real and an\n*explicit* rational. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_dyadic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_dyadic","kind":"theorem","line":452,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L452-L462","doc":"**Every bound of `α`'s expansion after `n` steps is a dyadic with denominator dividing\n`2ⁿ`.**\n\nThis is the piece that was missing: it names the `q` in `|α − m/q|`, so a run of length `k`\nat step `n` reads as an approximation of exponent `(n + k)/n` rather than merely as a small\nerror. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DyadicState.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DyadicState.step","kind":"theorem","line":411,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L411-L449","doc":"**One step at most doubles the denominator.**\n\nThe four cases split by regime rather than by sign: `±1` keeps the denominator (add\n`±2ⁿ` to the numerator), and the two bisecting cases average two level-`n` dyadics, which\nlands at level `n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.dyadicState_init","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.dyadicState_init","kind":"theorem","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L406-L409","doc":"`init` is dyadic at level `0` — every bound is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.DyadicState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.DyadicState","kind":"def","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L402-L404","doc":"All three bounds are dyadic at level `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsDyadicAt.succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsDyadicAt.succ","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L397-L400","doc":"A dyadic at level `n` is a dyadic at level `n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsDyadicAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsDyadicAt","kind":"def","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L388-L395","doc":"`x` is a dyadic rational with denominator dividing `2ⁿ`.\n\n⚠ Stated **multiplicatively** (`2ⁿ · x` is an integer) rather than as `x = m / 2ⁿ`.  The\ndivision form is the natural reading but it defeats `ring`: closing the step cases needs\n`2ⁿ / 2ⁿ = 1`, which `ring` cannot do without knowing `2ⁿ ≠ 0`, so every case would need\n`field_simp` and a side condition.  Multiplied through, all four cases are `ring`\nidentities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_plus_run","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_plus_run","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L359-L376","doc":"**`α` undershot at every step of the window ⟹ that window is a plus-run.**\n\nThe hypothesis is a statement about `α` — it says the expansion's value stayed below `α`\nfor `k` consecutive steps — and the conclusion puts `expandState` into the shape\n`run_plus_approximates` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_succ_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_succ_plus","kind":"theorem","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L352-L356","doc":"A step where the value undershoots `α` is a `+` step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.run_plus_approximates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.run_plus_approximates","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L300-L341","doc":"**The Liouville-shaped statement.**  After a run of `k` plus-signs, `α` is within\n`gap / 2ᵏ` of `st.hi` — a rational **fixed before the run began**.\n\nThe denominator is whatever `st.hi` already had; the accuracy improves by `2ᵏ` without it\ngrowing. That decoupling is what an approximation exponent above `1` means, and it is\nsupplied by the run rather than by the bisection rate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.foldl_replicate_plus_hi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.foldl_replicate_plus_hi","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L286-L298","doc":"**A run of `+` freezes the upper bound.**  Induction on the run length, using that each\nstep both preserves the bisection regime and leaves `hi` untouched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.step_plus_hi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.step_plus_hi","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L281-L284","doc":"A `+` step leaves the **upper** bound alone (it raises the lower one). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expansion_approximates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expansion_approximates","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L253-L265","doc":"**The bridge, in one statement.**  For *any* real `α`, once its expansion has bracketed,\n`k` further signs approximate `α` to within `gap / 2ᵏ`.\n\nThis is what `conj:diophantine-birthday`'s \"birthday **trajectory**\" needs on the surreal\nside: prefix length controls approximation quality, the denominator is exponential in the\nprefix length, and the target is a genuine given real rather than the expansion's own\nbracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_gap","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L232-L251","doc":"**The expansion's own bracket halves per sign.**\n\n`Bracketed.foldl_gap` says this for a `List.foldl`; `expandState` is defined by recursion\non `ℕ` instead, so the two need connecting.  They connect directly through\n`Bracketed.step` — no list bookkeeping required, because `expandState α (n+1)` is literally\none `step` applied to `expandState α n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.dist_le_gap_of_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.dist_le_gap_of_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L221-L229","doc":"**The payoff**: the expansion of `α`, once it has bracketed, approximates `α` to within\nits bracket width — and `Bracketed.foldl_gap` says that width halves per sign.\n\nThis is the statement `DiophantineBirthdayTrajectory` wanted and could not state: prefix\nlength controls approximation quality, with an exponential dyadic denominator, for a *given*\nreal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.dist_le_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.dist_le_gap","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L203-L219","doc":"**The approximation bound.**  When the state both brackets `α` and is in the bisection\nregime, its value is within the bracket width of `α`.\n\nBoth `α` and `value` lie in `[lo, hi]` — `α` by `Brackets`, `value` strictly by\n`Bracketed` — so they differ by at most the width. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_brackets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState_brackets","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L179-L201","doc":"**The expansion always brackets its target.**\n\nInduction on `n`.  The base case is vacuous — `init` has neither bound set — and each step\nre-establishes the invariant by construction: a `+` moves the *lower* bound up to a value\nknown to undershoot `α`, a `-` moves the *upper* bound down to one known not to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Brackets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Brackets","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L173-L176","doc":"`α` lies within the state's bracket — weakly, so that a rational `α` landing exactly on\na bound is covered rather than excluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.expandState","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L166-L171","doc":"The state after `n` signs of `α`'s own expansion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.gap_after_plus_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.gap_after_plus_minus","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L138-L152","doc":"**The rate, on a concrete sequence.**  Extending `[+, -]` by `k` further signs leaves a\nbracket of width `2⁻ᵏ`, since `[+, -]` brackets `(0, 1)` at width `1`.\n\nThis is the statement a Liouville comparison consumes: prefix length controls approximation\nquality exponentially, with the dyadic denominator that `2ⁿ` names. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.bracketed_plus_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.bracketed_plus_minus","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L132-L136","doc":"**The bisection regime is reached**, by the shortest sequence that reaches it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.gap_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.gap_pos","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L113-L118","doc":"The bracket stays positive, so the rate above is a genuine contraction rather than a\nstatement about an empty interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.foldl_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.foldl_gap","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L92-L111","doc":"**`n` signs shrink the bracket by `2ⁿ`.**\n\nThis is the rate the trajectory statement needs: prefix length `n` buys a bracket of width\n`gap₀ / 2ⁿ`, so the approximant is within `gap₀ / 2ⁿ⁺¹` of anything the bracket still\ncontains — a dyadic approximation whose denominator is exponential in the prefix length,\nwhich is exactly the quantity a Liouville exponent is measured against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.step","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L72-L90","doc":"**One sign halves the bracket**, and leaves the state in the bisection regime.\n\nBoth signs are covered: `+` keeps the upper bound and moves the lower one up to the old\nvalue; `-` keeps the lower bound and moves the upper one down. In each case the new\nbracket is exactly one half of the old, because the old value was its midpoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.GonshorState.gap","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L69-L70","doc":"The bracket width. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.lt","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.mid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.mid","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.hasHi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.hasHi","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.hasLo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.hasLo","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Bracketed","kind":"structure","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/GonshorConvergence.lean#L59-L67","doc":"The **bisection regime**: both bounds exist, the value lies strictly inside them, and\n— the clause that does the work — the value is the *midpoint* of its own bracket.\n\n`GonshorState.step` re-establishes this at every step, which is why the bracket halves. ","signatureChunk":0}]}